Carafe: with X87ConversionRounding, FLDCW leaves FPCR alone and conversions round by the guest's FCW.
Games built with MSVC convert floats to integers through _ftol, which sets the x87 rounding mode to truncation with
FLDCW, stores with FISTP and restores the mode with FLDCW. In reduced precision FEX wrote FPCR at both FLDCWs, and
writing FPCR stalls the A57; in a racing game _ftol and _controlfp were among the hottest functions. With the option,
FLDCW and FLDENV only store FCW, FIST and FISTP pick nearest, down, up or toward zero from FCW's rounding bits, and
FRNDINT does the same; x87 arithmetic always rounds to nearest. Off by default, reduced precision only.
MIT, as the files it changes.

